            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdomen due to acute pancreatitis--a rare presentation of leptospirosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>911-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Even though, Leptospiral infection is not uncommon, it can have different rare presentations. Acute pancreatitis is one such rare gastrointestinal manifestation of acute pancreatitis. Apart from the typical clinical features; elevated serum lipase or elastase-1, along with radiological evidence and positive leptospiral serology confirms this rare association.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
